The text of the acts in this repository is taken from the Revised Acts published by the Law Reform Commission of
Ireland (Coimisiún um Athchóiriú an Dlí), Styne House, Upper Hatch Street, Dublin 2, at
https://revisedacts.lawreform.ie. Each Revised Act states:

    This Revised Act is an administrative consolidation of the [Act]. It is prepared by the Law Reform Commission in
    accordance with its function under the Law Reform Commission Act 1975 (3/1975) to keep the law under review and
    to undertake revision and consolidation of statute law.

    Disclaimer: While every care has been taken in the preparation of this Revised Act, the Law Reform Commission can
    assume no responsibility for and give no guarantees, undertakings or warranties concerning the accuracy,
    completeness or up to date nature of the information provided and does not accept any liability whatsoever
    arising from any errors or omissions. Please notify any errors, omissions and comments by email to
    revisedacts@lawreform.ie.

Only the Acts as enacted, published on the electronic Irish Statute Book (www.irishstatutebook.ie), are the official
text; a Revised Act is not.

Reuse terms. The Law Reform Commission's Open Data Licence
(https://revisedacts.lawreform.ie/open-data-licence) applies the Oireachtas (Open Data) PSI Licence to Legislative
Text on the Revised Acts website and the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International Licence (CC BY 4.0) to its
Annotation Text. The two forms of text have separate creators and separate attribution statements:

    Contains Oireachtas Copyright Material, reproduced with the permission of the Houses of the Oireachtas under the Oireachtas (Open Data) PSI Licence

    Contains Law Reform Commission Annotation Text, licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International Licence (CC BY 4.0)

Changed: split into one file per provision, annotation marks removed, layout normalised, and arranged as a history
of commits. These changes do not alter the source licences. The repository remains private unless its owner decides
otherwise.

Everything else in this repository (the history as commits, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) is
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
